Found 2026-09-01 by the orchestrator while reviewing karr #127 (AKI bare `reasoning` key lifted onto Response.thinking, chat_response only).

State of the code (HEAD 07f6d68):
- Langertha::Stream::Chunk has no `thinking` attribute (grep thinking|reasoning in Stream/Chunk.pm, Stream.pm, Role/Streaming.pm: 0 hits).
- Role::OpenAICompatible::parse_stream_chunk (~line 481) reads only $choice->{delta}{content}. Every streamed `delta.reasoning_content` (DeepSeek, NousResearch, xAI, ...) and `delta.reasoning` (AKI, OpenRouter) is discarded.
- The non-streaming path DOES surface it: OpenAICompatible::chat_response:371 (reasoning_content), AKIOpenAI around chat_response (reasoning, k127), AnthropicCompatible::chat_response:303 (thinking blocks).

Consequence: $response->thinking is populated for simple_chat but silently undef for simple_chat_stream / simple_chat_stream_realtime_f on the same engine and prompt. Same class of asymmetry as k125 (cached_tokens visible on one route only).

Design shape (needs a decision before code, NOT a one-liner):
1. Stream::Chunk gains a `thinking` (Maybe[Str]) field, parallel to `content` / `tool_calls`.
2. Each dialect stream parser fills it from its own delta spelling: OpenAI-family `delta.reasoning_content` (+ AKI/OpenRouter `delta.reasoning` - decide whether the AKI-scoped override pattern from k127 extends to the stream parser), Anthropic `content_block_delta` with `thinking_delta`, Gemini parts with `thought: true`, Ollama `message.thinking` (native /api/chat with think=true).
3. The aggregation into the final Response (Role::Chat, where aggregate_tool_calls lives) concatenates thinking the way it concatenates content, so the streamed Response ends up with the same ->thinking as the non-streamed one.
4. Streaming callbacks: decide whether thinking chunks are delivered to the user callback (as chunk->thinking) or only aggregated.

The langertha-llm-advisor is asked to verify the per-provider delta spellings before anyone implements. Relates: k127 (non-streaming AKI lift), ADR 0011 (ttft is only observable on the async stream path - thinking-first-token likely the same).


