## Findings on the NON-STREAMING path (this is bigger than the streaming gap)

The ticket asked whether any dialect's non-streaming path already reads the wrong spelling. Four do.

1. **`Role::OpenAICompatible::chat_response:371` reads ONLY `$msg->{reasoning_content}`.**
   Five shipped engines put their reasoning under the bare `reasoning` key and are therefore
   silently blank on `$response->thinking` today, on the NON-streamed route:
   `Engine::vLLM` + `Engine::VLLMHook`, `Engine::Groq`, `Engine::Cerebras`, `Engine::OpenRouter`.
   vLLM is the sharp one -- its own docs carry a migration warning: "`reasoning` used to be called
   `reasoning_content` ... your client code could silently read an EMPTY `reasoning_content` even
   when `reasoning` is populated." That is exactly the failure mode here.
   `Engine::AKIOpenAI` already has the AKI-scoped `around chat_response` lift from k127 -- it is
   the only engine that does. Minimal fix: read `reasoning_content`, else `reasoning` (guard
   `!ref` so OpenRouter's `reasoning_details` ARRAY never lands in a Str attribute), in the shared
   role, and drop the AKI-scoped override as redundant.

2. **`Engine::Ollama::chat_response:~315` never reads `message.thinking` at all.**
   Ollama's NATIVE path drops thinking on BOTH routes, not just streaming. The streaming half is
   what this ticket is about; the non-streaming half is a separate one-liner.

3. **`Role::AnthropicCompatible::chat_response:303` filters `grep { $_->{type} eq 'thinking' }`.**
   Anthropic's docs warn against precisely this: "If your code filters content blocks by type
   (for example, `block.type == "thinking"`) when round-tripping responses with tool use, also
   include `redacted_thinking` blocks. Filtering on `block.type == "thinking"` alone silently
   drops `redacted_thinking` blocks and breaks the multi-turn protocol."
   Langertha's tool loop is safe here BY LUCK, because `Role::Tools::format_tool_results` echoes
   `$data->{content}` verbatim (the whole raw block array) for `tool_wire_format eq 'anthropic'`
   rather than rebuilding it -- keep it that way. But `$response->thinking` itself never surfaces
   redacted blocks.
   Bigger: on CURRENT Claude models `thinking.display` defaults to `"omitted"` (Opus 4.7/4.8/5,
   Sonnet 5, Fable 5/5.1, Mythos 5/5.1), which means NO `thinking_delta` events are emitted and
   the thinking text is empty -- only the `signature` is populated. So a stream parser that fills
   `thinking` from `thinking_delta` will legitimately get nothing on today's default config;
   `display:"summarized"` has to be requested. Anything asserting non-empty thinking on Anthropic
   needs that set.

4. **`Engine::Gemini::parse_stream_chunk:~534` reads `$parts->[0]->{text}` -- the FIRST PART ONLY.**
   Two bugs in one line, both live today, independent of any new `thinking` field:
   (a) when part 0 is a thought part, its text is emitted AS CONTENT (thought summary leaks into
       `$chunk->content`);
   (b) when part 0 is a thought part and part 1 is the real answer, the answer is DROPPED.
   Non-streaming `Engine::Gemini::chat_response:~380` does it correctly (loops all parts, splits
   on `$part->{thought}`). The stream parser should be brought to the same shape.
   Also load-bearing for tool calling: Gemini's docs say the signature "might be returned in a
   part with empty text content, so be sure to parse all parts until `finish_reason` is returned."

## Design correction to the ticket's step 3

The ticket says "the aggregation into the final Response ... so the streamed Response ends up with
the same ->thinking as the non-streamed one". There IS no streamed Response today.
`Role::Chat::chat_stream_realtime_f` returns `($content, \@all_chunks, \%timing)` and
`simple_chat_stream` returns a plain joined string -- no `Langertha::Response` is ever built on the
stream path. So step 3 has to be respecified as either
  (a) an `aggregate_thinking(\@chunks)` helper mirroring the existing `aggregate_tool_calls`
      (Role::Chat:675), returned alongside content, or
  (b) a separate decision to start returning a Response from the stream path.
(a) is the surgical one and matches the existing seam.

## Type hazard that will bite the implementer (Mistral)

`Langertha::Response.content` and `Langertha::Stream::Chunk.content` are both `isa => 'Str',
required => 1`. Mistral's reasoning models return `message.content` as an ARRAY of chunks
(ThinkChunk + TextChunk) and `delta.content` as an ARRAY during the thinking phase. Feeding that
through `Role::OpenAICompatible::chat_response` (`content => $msg->{content} // ''`) or
`parse_stream_chunk` (`content => $choice->{delta}{content} // ''`) is a Moose type-constraint
death, not a silent drop. `Engine::Mistral`'s `default_model` is `mistral-small-latest`
(non-reasoning) so nobody has hit it, but Mistral's docs say the native `magistral-*` line is
deprecated in favour of reasoning in the mainline models. Whoever implements #129 should decide
whether to normalize a list-shaped `content` (join the TextChunks, route the ThinkChunk to
`thinking`) in the same change. Filed separately if it is not in scope here.

## Round-trip obligations -- the reason this is not cosmetic

Several providers REQUIRE the reasoning to be sent back, and two of them fail hard:

- **DeepSeek: HTTP 400.** "all prior turns' `reasoning_content` must be sent back" when `tools`
  is present. Without `tools` it is ignored.
- **Moonshot / Kimi:** k3 has always-on preserved thinking; within one tool-call loop all
  `reasoning_content` must be sent back. (`Engine::Moonshot::default_model` is `kimi-k3`.)
- **Anthropic:** "when you return tool results, you must pass the thinking blocks from the
  assistant message back to the API, complete and unmodified"; modified blocks -> 400.
- **Gemini 3:** missing `thoughtSignature` in a function-calling turn -> 400, and there is a
  dedicated `finishReason: MISSING_THOUGHT_SIGNATURE`.
- **OpenRouter:** `reasoning_details` must be round-tripped unmodified and in original order.
- **xAI:** dropping `reasoning_content` costs the prompt-cache hit.
- **Mistral:** stripping the ThinkChunk "significantly degrades output quality".

`Role::Tools::format_tool_results` echoes the RAW provider structure for the `anthropic`,
`gemini` and `responses` dialects (safe), but the `openai` default branch REBUILDS the assistant
echo from exactly three keys:

    { role => 'assistant', content => $choice->{message}{content},
      tool_calls => $choice->{message}{tool_calls} }

so `reasoning_content` / `reasoning` / `reasoning_details` are dropped on every OpenAI-dialect
engine. Per the DeepSeek doc that is a hard 400 on the second iteration of a tool loop against a
DeepSeek thinking model, and a correctness/quality loss on Kimi, OpenRouter and Mistral. The
`ollama` branch rebuilds the same way and drops `message.thinking`.
That is a SEPARATE and higher-severity bug than the streaming gap this ticket tracks -- filed as
its own karr ticket so #129 stays scoped to the stream parsers.
